# Git commit permissions

This machine signs commits with GPG. The sandbox cannot talk to `gpg-agent` (`~/.gnupg`), so a sandboxed `git commit` fails with `gpg: can't connect to the agent: Operation not permitted`.

When creating a commit (or any other GPG-signed git command):

- Request `required_permissions: ["all"]` on the **first** attempt.
- Do not try a sandboxed commit first, then retry.
- Do not pass `--no-gpg-sign` or skip hooks to work around this.
